::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q01::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6<br><br>Question:<br>Describe g(x)=f(x)+3. {
= Shift up 3#Correct. Adding outside changes outputs upward.
~ Shift down 3#That would be f(x)-3.
~ Shift left 3#Horizontal shifts happen inside the input.
~ Shift right 3#That would involve f(x-3).
}

::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q02::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6<br><br>Question:<br>Describe g(x)=f(x-4). {
~ Shift left 4#Inside shifts use the opposite sign.
= Shift right 4#Correct. Subtracting inside the input shifts the graph right.
~ Shift up 4#Vertical shifts occur outside.
~ Reflect across x-axis#Reflection would use a negative outside.
}

::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q03::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6<br><br>Question:<br>Describe g(x)=-f(x). {
~ Reflect across the y-axis#That would be f(-x).
~ Shift down 1#A negative is not a vertical shift.
= Reflect across the x-axis#Correct. A negative outside changes output signs.
~ Shift right 1#A negative outside is not horizontal.
}

::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q04::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6<br><br>Question:<br>Describe g(x)=f(x+2)-5. {
~ Shift right 2 and down 5#Inside signs reverse.
~ Shift left 2 and up 5#The outside -5 shifts down.
~ Shift right 5 and down 2#This mixes the values.
= Shift left 2 and down 5#Correct. Adding inside shifts left; subtracting outside shifts down.
}

::ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q05::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L04_GP_Q05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6<br><br>Question:<br>Which rule shifts f left 6? {
= g(x)=f(x+6)#Correct. Adding inside shifts left.
~ g(x)=f(x-6)#This shifts right 6.
~ g(x)=f(x)+6#This shifts up 6.
~ g(x)=f(x)-6#This shifts down 6.
}

